title: Slack stops receiving messages after a brief network disconnect; detect and recover automatically
updated_at: "2026-11-02T06:11:30Z"
---
User report: A brief drop in the network connection used by Clawq can disconnect Slack, after which incoming Slack messages no longer reach Clawq.

Reproduction: With the Slack connector running, briefly interrupt network connectivity, restore it, then send a Slack message to Clawq. Check whether inbound delivery resumes without restarting Clawq.

Expected behavior: Detect a lost or stale Slack connection, expose the disconnected/reconnecting state accurately in status and logs, and automatically reconnect with bounded retry/backoff when connectivity returns. Incoming messages sent after recovery must be processed normally without a manual daemon restart or duplicate processing.

Acceptance criteria:
- Exercise a brief network interruption and a stale/half-open connection.
- Verify disconnect detection and automatic reconnect through the production Slack connector path.
- Verify inbound message delivery resumes after network restoration.
- Add regression coverage for disconnect/reconnect and observable connector health.

The precise failure mechanism and treatment of messages sent during the outage require investigation; do not assume Slack replays missed events.